      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thank you for your comment.\nAs you guess, the reason to use string is to set \u003cempty\u003e for its default value and to manage this configuration with only 1 resource.\n0 is FRAME_RATE_COMPATIBILITY_DEFAULT and another number may also conflict in the future.\nSo, I thought integer resource was not good for 1 resouce solution.\n\nIt is also possible to have 2 resources, where 1 bool resource for enable/disable and 1 integer value for overlaid frame rate values.\nShould I change this commit to 2 resource solution?",
